how are you feeling about how everything  went down  um i kind of expected that this week  might be my week to go it sucked but i  felt like a fifth wheel um so hearing  that i had a little chance to stay in  the game with kevin i was like seem to  be changing his mind a little bit that  gave me a little bit of hope so having  that crushed hurt a little bit i'm not  gonna lie but i feel like i was  preparing myself i felt like it might be  my time to go this week so it wasn't a  shock by any means  you were the holder of the the secret  power of veto this season do you have  any regrets  i actually don't i really don't regret  not using it i feel like at the time  that gino and i talked about it so many  times that it wouldn't make sense to  back door marty because i think as soon  as you back door marty the showmance is  going on the block next for the next  stop as the target so it didn't make  sense to get rid of marty it made sense  to use him as a shield  we didn't know that he was going to use  gummy bears to make decisions the weak  following  but um no regrets all good i don't know  regrets now you got the shock of  lifetime uh with a surprise visit from  your mom  yes i did that was the best was the best  part  of that surprise visit  yeah i think just getting to hear that  everyone back home was watching um  everyone back home is okay they're  rooting for me i have obviously didn't  win an hoh all season so i had not  gotten to hear from my family or friends  back home so just getting to hear that  from my mom was so amazing  and it seems like she gave gino the seal  of approval  a little bit my sister going into the  game was like don't be the idiot that  falls for the guy and gets all wrapped  up in the guy she's 16 years old okay  and she put me in my place so i asked my  mom i was like what does janelise think  about me meeting a boy in there my mom  said she loves it so hopefully that's  the case  that's amazing what do you what do you  think the future holds for the two of  you once this is all over  um it's a great question i don't think  we're not trying to put pressure on any  of it i think the feelings are  definitely real the experience we shared  was so unique and i think we definitely  put a relationship to the test in that  house living with the person for that  many days 24 hours a day so it's looking  good but we're not putting pressure on  anything just kind of seeing where it  goes having fun  now during your speech you said you  don't understand why nobody has the guts  to evict betty or josh  about those two that you think has  worked so well in their favor  i don't know what goes on with those two  they've been on the block so many times  together and apart and every single time  they escape the block i don't know what  is going on obviously now it it makes  more sense to me knowing that kevin  alina and josh had a final three or  whatever kevin said in his goodbye  message to me that makes more sense but  it's just like how have we managed to  let these people slide through like this  every time they're on the block it hurts  me it really does  now you had a real obsession with the  red door you even mentioned it on your  way out of the house if you had to guess  if you had to guess what do you think is  behind the red door i don't know why i  have this feeling i had a nightmare  about the red door i had many but i just  have this feeling the red door went off  in the middle of the night there were  strobe lights there was smoke coming out  of the door and i'm i think door number  12 because we're missing door number 12  in the house i think it's behind that  door it's going to come into play  somewhere  it might be a ridiculous thing to think  but i don't know anything so that's what  i'm going with  and now what is your strategy going into  jury like will you still be playing the  game or do you plan to  let your guard down a little like what  are you thinking  um obviously when it comes down to  choosing the winner i think it's a huge  decision it's a life-changing decision  so  i would love to be logical and strategic  about it i don't want to use my emotions  because i've said the entire game  emotional players  really get on my nerves so i definitely  want to unpack all of my emotions  currently and not make like a spiteful  decision i want to make sure that i'm  voting for somebody who i really think  deserves it  so who's the next person that you want  to see  walking through the jury house doors and  who do you not want to see join the jury  i don't want to see kevin  i'm sorry i don't want to see kevin i  want kevin to win this game honestly  which might be surprising because he's  backstabbed me a couple of times but i  would love to see kev win i would love  to see helena come through those jury  doors as much as i don't really want to  talk to her right now i would love to  see her come through the jury doors so  kevin is  kevin knows who you want to win do you  think  that given the way things are going that  kevin is  the person who's going to take it  i think he has a great chance of going  all the way to finals because everybody  seems to want to take kevin to final two  everyone seems to think that they have  the best chance sitting next to kevin  now coming into jury hearing what  everyone has to say it seems like  everybody wants kevin to win so i think  that people are going to bring kevin to  finale night  and i think they might be surprised how  the jury votes i don't know  very interesting now if you could sum up  your whole experience  here on big brother canada in one word  what would it be  i'm going i'm it's a real toss-up  between enlightening and chaotic but i'm  gonna go with enlightenment it was an  enlightening experience overall  right but there's but there's definitely  elements of both for sure totally yes  totally chaotic  right on well listen um i'm so excited  to see what's happening next uh great  talking to you thanks for taking the  time yeah thanks so much for having me  you

